From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:34:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] soc/intel/alderlake: Read the TME option once on the
 BSP

soc_core_init() runs on every core, and each core looked up the
"intel_tme" option itself. With a backend such as the EFI variable
store, every lookup parses the store, so all APs did that at once.
Read the option once in pre_mp_init(), before the APs start, and use
the result on every core.

[Generated by Claude, an AI model by Anthropic.]

Signed-off-by: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
---
 src/soc/intel/alderlake/cpu.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/alderlake/cpu.c b/src/soc/intel/alderlake/cpu.c
index 88ce4017..7b6a6bcf 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/alderlake/cpu.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/alderlake/cpu.c
@@ -107,6 +107,8 @@ bool soc_is_nominal_freq_supported(void)
 	return true;
 }
 
+static bool tme_enable;
+
 /* All CPUs including BSP will run the following function. */
 void soc_core_init(struct device *cpu)
 {
@@ -141,7 +143,7 @@ void soc_core_init(struct device *cpu)
 	/* Enable Turbo */
 	enable_turbo();
 
-	if (get_uint_option("intel_tme", CONFIG(INTEL_TME)) && is_tme_supported())
+	if (tme_enable)
 		set_tme_core_activate();
 }
 
@@ -155,6 +157,9 @@ static void pre_mp_init(void)
 {
 	soc_fsp_load();
 
+	/* Read once on the BSP: an option lookup per AP can be slow (e.g. EFI variable store) */
+	tme_enable = get_uint_option("intel_tme", CONFIG(INTEL_TME)) && is_tme_supported();
+
 	const config_t *conf = config_of_soc();
 	if (conf->enable_energy_perf_pref) {
 		if (check_energy_perf_cap())
